# sha256 of the outputs of build_assets.sh: the asset sets assets-ssfar4f (recommended since 15 October 2026, evening,
# the chosen default: ssfar4eu with the plain catch fence, no fence rule), assets-ssfar4eu (the set before it: every
# sign of the sign sheet super-sampled, no mip chain on a super-sampled sign word), assets-ssfar4e (before that:
# road decals on or above the road, super-sampled signs), assets-ssfar4cf3r (the rock decal cores), assets-ssfar4cf3
# (the three-level catch fence), assets-ssfar4c, assets-ssfar4b and the candidates assets-ssfar4d and assets-ssfar4bf3
# (build/dc-native-ss-far.eSWVWs, dc-native-fence-sweep.PrBsVt), and the generated headers of the ELF build. Hashes
# only: no ROM data. build_assets.sh compares OUTDIR/outputs.sha256 with this. The ELFs' loaded images depend on the
# source tree, not only on these inputs, so they are not listed here.
# 15 October (slot machine): world.dnm/world.dnt of every set (ssfar4b, c, cf3, cf3r, e and the candidates d, bf3)
# carry the slot machine reels (prepare_world_objects.py: 64 reel models x 3 faces, three PLACED instances, kinds
# SLOT..SLOT+2); nothing else in them changed (same composites, palette banks 56 of 58; ssfar4e: the same 501 streak
# faces draped, 68 raised; ssfar4d: the same 67 faces baked). The candidates' rows before were older builds' (the
# recipe without the reels made other world packs for them, ssfar4bf3's strips = ssfar4cf3's); these are a run from
# the ROM (build/dc-native-slot.assets-e, --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3: 1063 identical).
# 15 October (signs-union merged onto the reels): lod_groups.py keys far materials by the whole record, so
# assets-ssfar4e world.dnm/world.dnt change by exactly the 15 super-sampled far faces that carried another
# material's light (2064 x3, 2070 x6, 3594 x6; 3 more material records, every other face, vertex, strip and level-of-
# detail group the same as the reel build); every other row unchanged. A run from the ROM
# (build/dc-native-integrate.recipe, --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3,ssfar4eu: 1061 identical, these 2 different).
# 15 October (ssfar4eu recommended): assets-ssfar4eu is built always (rows added from that run; its world packs carry
# the reels and the lighting fix; every other file of the set is ssfar4e's).
# 15 October (wrong way a818): the HUD pack carries the wrong-way message (block 2876914 "逆走" of table 236830[1],
# prepare_hud.py): headers/hud/hud_data.h and every set's hud/sheet-0.dt change (hud.dp and sheet-1.dt the same).
# A run from the ROM (build/dc-native-wrongway.recipe, --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3,ssfar4eu: 1209 identical).
# 15 October (car damage): every set gains car-damage.dnb (tools/prepare_damage_bodies.py: the player's 16 damaged
# bodies as position/normal variants of the clean body's mesh); no other row changes (car.dnm, car.dnt and the
# headers are the same: the damaged bodies are not catalogue entries). A run from the ROM on dreamcast-native 0f0eeb5
# (build/dc-native-cardamage.recipeF, --elf --check --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3: 1355 identical, these 9 added).
# 15 October (CONDITION panel, time extension): the HUD pack carries the CONDITION panel (12c98..13208: the icons of
# the player and of the opponents as sprites, the panel's place and colour, the fitted panel projection) and the
# "TIME EXTENSION!!" message of ae98 (block 2872c42), prepare_hud.py on a HUD trace that now carries the panel's
# fields (tools/trace_hud.hpp): headers/hud/hud_data.h and every set's hud/hud.dp, hud/sheet-0.dt and hud/sheet-1.dt
# change (28 rows); nothing else. Made from the ROM by the recipe's two HUD steps (trace_hud with this checkout's
# trace_hud.hpp, then prepare_hud.py), whose earlier prepare_hud.py gives the four previous hashes from that trace.
# 15 October (car effects: dust and sparks): car.dnm of every set carries the player's punch-through car effects
# (include/car_effects.h: dust 231f06[1..31] and sparks 232006[9..24], 47 models of 1-4 faces, 134 faces; instances
# between the catalogue and the player's six parts, tools/append_player_parts.py --effects), car.dnt their 10 textures
# (64x64 PAL4, 20,480 bytes of VRAM) and 10 bindings (luma 255; palettes 54 as before), headers/race-header/
# intro_drive_data.h the 47 catalogue entries. Every world pack, car-damage.dnb and every other row is the same. A run
# from the ROM (build/dc-native-fx.recipe, --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3: 1345 identical, these 19 different).
# 17 October (views VR1..VR4, rebased on the manual transmission): headers/race-start-data/race_start_data.h gains
# the four view presets (2320b6) and the pit tracks of every view (234a9c/234aac[501710]); car.dnm of every set the clean
# hoods of the hood view, 94fff9 and the manual 9506a8 (231eb0[v][0], tools/append_player_parts.py --hoods: two
# instances after the crew), car.dnt their textures and lumas (the race-car export lists all eight hoods,
# tools/export_course.hpp), every set's new car-hoods.dnb the automatic car's four hoods as variants of the clean hood's
# mesh (tools/prepare_damage_bodies.py --hoods), headers/race-header/intro_drive_data.h the two catalogue entries.
# Made by the recipe's own commands on build/dc-native-gears.recipe's intermediates (build/dc-native-views.work/
# car_hoods.sh, which reproduces that run's car.dnm, car.dnt, car-damage.dnb and race header without --hoods); the
# ssfar4bf and ssfar4f world palettes with the new car.dnt are byte-identical; the other sets' world rows not rerun.
# 18 October (gear indicator b0c0, branch gear-hud on c7d6f80): the HUD pack carries the manual races' gear indicator
# (the lever blocks 23263c, the brackets, "SHIFT" and the digits in colour 0x84; tools/prepare_hud.py places them after
# every other sprite): headers/hud/hud_data.h and every set's hud/hud.dp (bank 2 gains the digits' yellow) and
# hud/sheet-2.dt change, hud/sheet-3.dt is new (bank 0's lever sprites); sheet-0.dt and sheet-1.dt are the same.
# prepare_hud.py on the HUD traces of build/dc-native-expert.recipe (whose previous prepare_hud.py gives every
# previous hash of the pack byte for byte), not a whole recipe run.
# 30 October (rolling start overlay, branch gaps-2): the HUD pack carries the banner, its car, ACCEL ON!, AUTO DRIVE, the
# digits and GO! of ab78 and d438 (tools/prepare_hud.py, after every other sprite; the banner's stipple is not in its art):
# headers/hud/hud_data.h and every set's hud/hud.dp (bank 2 gains 11 colours), hud/sheet-2.dt and hud/sheet-3.dt change,
# hud/sheet-4.dt is new; sheet-0.dt and sheet-1.dt are the same. prepare_hud.py on the three HUD traces of this checkout.
# 30 October (lap message ad34, branch gaps-2): BEST LAP, LAP TIME and the time's font in the same pack, which takes banks
# 60..63 (--first-bank 60 --max-banks 4): hud_data.h and every set's hud.dp, sheet-1.dt (BEST LAP on its free rows),
# sheet-2.dt, sheet-3.dt, sheet-4.dt change; sheet-0.dt is the same.
# 30 October (the map's second-car marker, branch gaps-2): prepare_hud.py --second-marker 1 on a new HUD trace (13000 frames
# of the Expert finishing race, step trace_hud_lead): MARKER_SECOND and a copy of the player's marker; hud_data.h also holds
# each map's marker turn and size. hud_data.h, hud.dp, sheet-3.dt change (sheet-3 grows to 256x256).
