# 15 October, night (music in every set): build_assets.sh --music ARCHIVE runs build_music.sh as its first step and
# copies tNN.afb and tNN.afx of the 45 tracks into music/ of every set (90 rows a set, 810 added for the nine sets;
# the same hashes as those files' rows of music-expected.sha256: vgmrips' pack ac086fd5..., AICAflow c6b116dd,
# AICAforge e77de852). No other row changed. A run from the ROM and the pack on next 913fa26 + this change
# (build/dc-native-music.recipe, --elf --check --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3: 1364 identical before the rows were added,
# all 2174 after; deleted after the check). With --no-music the music rows are reported as one line.
# 16 October (integrate2: dreamcast-native 93775e0 with the radar HUD pack, + fx-dust-sparks + music-handoff): the rows
# of the three branches touch different files (HUD 28 rows already here, car effects 19 changed, music 810 added) and
# merge without a conflict. A run from the ROM and the pack on this tree (build/dc-native-int2.recipe, --music --elf
# --check --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3): 2174 identical, 0 different, 0 not built; no row changed by the merge.
# 16 October (car effects: smoke and spin smoke): car.dnm of every set carries the checker car effects too (include/
# car_effects.h: smoke 231f86[1..31] and the four spin-smoke lists of 232206, 35 models, 206 faces; after the dust and
# sparks, tools/append_player_parts.py --effects), car.dnt their 5 textures (64x64 PAL4, 10,240 bytes of VRAM) and 14
# bindings of the translucent class (tools/prepare_palette_materials.py: vertex alpha 0x80, entry 15 alpha 0; palettes
# 54 as before), headers/race-header/intro_drive_data.h the 35 catalogue entries. Every world pack, car-damage.dnb, the
# music and every other row is the same. A run from the ROM and the music pack on branch fx-smoke
# (build/dc-native-smoke.recipe, --music --variants ssfar4d,ssfar4bf3: 2155 identical, these 19 different).
# 16 October (pit stop, build/dc-native-pitimpl.recipe): headers/race-start-data/race_start_data.h (the pit tables
# nm_race_pit, the pit camera tracks 234a9c[2]/234aac[2] and nm_race_keyed_tracks, prepare_intro.py --race-start) and
# the HUD pack with "PIT WORK!" ab2c (headers/hud/hud_data.h, every set's hud/hud.dp, hud/sheet-0.dt, hud/sheet-1.dt):
# 29 rows; the other 2145 identical.
# 17 October (manual transmission, branch gears, build/dc-native-gears.recipe): car.dnm of every set carries the pit
# crew's manual twins (the 16 lists 64 bytes after each crew model set, 1ad3c with 501464 = 1: 12 more models; 38 crew
# instances instead of 26), car.dnt their 22 bindings (no new texture, palettes as before),
# headers/race-header/intro_drive_data.h the 12 catalogue entries (15 rows); headers/script-manual/race_script_data.h
# is new (the manual race, recipes/inputs/inputs-manual.txt, tests/test_manual_lockstep.py PASS). The fast race's
